  "description": "Multifunction power meter (Delta Energy EMD96): voltages, currents, powers, power factor, frequency, energies and demands as input registers, with the settings as holding registers",
  "revision": 2,
  "revised": "2026-11-15",
  "source": "Ziegler / Delta Energy Systems, Manual EMD96 (multifunction meter), section 9 RS 485 (Modbus)",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Delta Energy Manual EMD96",
      "url": "https://github.com/user-attachments/files/34887681/Ziegler-Delat-Energy.Manual-EMD96._.PDF._.Ac.Power._.Transformer.pdf",
      "note": "Section 9, tables 4 and 5; attached to issue #378",
      "accessed": "2026-11-15",
      "sha256": "c1841ca1fedf2f1fa8070648fb324a7e56c669042374d40e200e88b313d61719"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU, 2-wire RS-485, 2400 to 19200 baud (set from the front panel or with the RS-485 set-up code), address 1 to 247, even, odd or no parity. Input registers (function 04) hold the measurements and holding registers (03, 16) the settings.",
    "Every value is a 32-bit IEEE 754 float in two registers. A read can ask for 20 parameters at most. The default order is most significant word first; writing 2141.0 to the word order register switches it.",
    "Addresses are the manual's start addresses (30001 is address 0 and 40001 is address 0), written in decimal.",
    "The manual ticks which parameters exist on 3-phase 4-wire, 3-phase 3-wire and single-phase systems; the descriptions say where a parameter is not available.",
    "The 20 user-assignable registers (0x200 to 0x226) are not listed.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
